# Elite Documentation Sync

- Any architecture/runtime/pipeline change must update:
  - `README.md`
  - `docs/architecture.md`
  - `docs/readiness.md`
  - `docs/phase-gates.md`
  - `docs/product-roadmap.md` (when UX milestone status changes)
  - `docs/desktop-workflow-mapping.md` (when component map changes)
  - relevant app READMEs
- Framework/catalog pin changes must update `pnpm-workspace.yaml` and note version in `README.md` + `docs/ui-port-plan.md` supply chain section.
- **Desktop UX port** changes must update:
  - `docs/ui-port-plan.md` (phase status)
  - `docs/desktop-workflow-mapping.md`
  - `docs/spec/feature-catalog.md` (UI-facing rows)
- Use precise status language:
  - `implemented` only when code exists
  - `validated` only when corresponding checks were executed
  - `100% complete` only when all local and remote gates are proven
- Split gates explicitly:
  - **Core Parity backend** — command matrix + SQLite/FTS + parity/hardening
  - **UX release gate** — per `docs/product-roadmap.md` and `docs/spec/native-e2e-checklist.md`
  - **AINative** — blocked until UX Parity Build Gate
- Never leave stale statements that conflict with current code.
